'''Crazed Moneko''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that was added in [[Version 6.10 Update|Version 6.10]]. Unlocked by beating the [[Crazed Moneko]] appearing on the '''28th''' of every month.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 418
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Crazed Moneko
|name2 = Corrupted Moneko
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Corrupted Moneko''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Being able to be used on 4-Crown stages is her biggest advantage over [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cheerleader Cat]], who outclasses her in terms of range and attack damage. What she lacks in those she makes up with her higher health and shorter delay between attacks. If not for being another guaranteed [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critter]], her best use is in her [[Cat Combo]] [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]], which increases the Critical rate of all units that can do Criticals. Its effect is most noticeable on fast attackers with a low Crit rate like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] or [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]].

Her range is lower than Cheerleader Cat's, but it is still high enough to outrange every single common [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy, earning her a spot in any [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|Anti-Metal]] lineup. Additionally, her attack rate is fast enough that as long as she is properly protected, she can deal lethal strikes to Metal enemies consistently. Plus, she’s cheap and you will probably be bringing her combo anyway, so you can just chuck her out on the field and hope for a crit every now and then.

{{Job|Classification = Critter & Combo Slave}}

